---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Next Move – Glenn Edley"
  description="Find what's stopping more sales, choose one useful move, and put it to the test with Glenn Edley. A paid working pilot for business owners and leaders."
  canonicalPath="/the-next-move/"
>
  <main class="next-move">
    <span class="back"><a href="/">← Glenn Edley</a></span>

    <header class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Next Move · working pilot</p>
      <h1>You want more sales. Where are they getting stuck?</h1>
      <p class="lead">You might know the change you want to make, but it hasn't happened. Or you're doing plenty and still can't see which part of the journey is holding sales back.</p>
      <p>I look at how people find you, decide to buy, buy again, and tell someone else. Then we choose one commercial move, test it quickly, and keep checking what actually happens.</p>
      <a class="action" href="#enquire">Tell me what's happening <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <p class="small">Two paid pilot places · NZ$1,500 + GST · Six weeks of follow-through</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="recognise">
      <h2 id="recognise">Does this sound familiar?</h2>
      <p>Enquiries come in, but the follow-up is patchy. People click, then disappear. Good customers rarely hear from you again. A new campaign or tool seems like the answer, yet you're not sure where the sale is being lost.</p>
      <p>Or perhaps you've already spotted the move: a better sales conversation, an offer, a referral system, or a way to bring customers back. It keeps slipping behind the daily work.</p>
      <p>Either is a useful starting point. We begin with the business result you want, not a prescribed channel or a long report.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="belief">
      <h2 id="belief">Nothing happens without a sale</h2>
      <p>My dad told me that when I was young. It has guided my work ever since. Sales don't begin when somebody talks to a salesperson. They begin when a customer becomes aware of you and continue through every interaction that earns a return visit or a recommendation.</p>
      <p>I call the way I examine that whole path the <strong>Customer First Framework</strong>. We follow the customer, look for the point where momentum breaks, and decide what is worth changing first. Sometimes the answer is in the message or website. Sometimes it is in a form, a handoff, a conversation, a missed follow-up, or customers you already have.</p>
      <p class="pull">Build buyers, not lists.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how">
      <h2 id="how">One move. A useful result quickly.</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Start with the goal.</strong>
          <span>What would need to be different in 12 months for this to have been a success? You share the relevant numbers, materials and your view of what's stopping you. I review the parts of the customer and sales journey that matter to that question.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Choose the first move together.</strong>
          <span>In a 90-minute working session, we identify the likely bottleneck, pick one change, name who will do it, and decide what we'll watch. You leave with a decision and a first action you can put to the test within five working days.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Do it. See what happens. Adjust.</strong>
          <span>Over five weekly 30-minute calls, we check the work, the response and the next action. Six weeks is the follow-through period; it isn't how long you wait to get something useful.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="small">For example: if people click an email but don't enquire, the next move might be to inspect the page, the form and what happens after it. It might be to call a small group of people who already showed interest. We choose from the evidence in your business, not from a standard list of tactics.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="roles">
      <h2 id="roles">How we work together</h2>
      <p><strong>My part:</strong> ask the questions, examine the relevant journey, bring commercial judgment, help choose and sequence a move, and review what happens.</p>
      <p><strong>Your part:</strong> make the change, or give someone in your business the time and authority to do it. If implementation needs outside help, we discuss that separately. We agree on one move and its boundaries before starting.</p>
      <p>At the end we decide whether to keep going, change direction, or stop. There is no automatic extension.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="evidence">
      <h2 id="evidence">Why I work this way</h2>
      <p>I've spent more than 20 years working on customer communication and commercial problems across retail and service businesses. I've brought the people responsible for marketing, sales and systems into a room, started with the business objective, and looked for the connection nobody had made yet.</p>
      <p>At <strong>Noel Leeming</strong>, an observation about the customer relationship contributed to the My Noel Leeming initiative and the communication that followed. The work did not stop with an idea on a whiteboard.</p>
      <p>In work with a <strong>big box retailer</strong>, email's share of website traffic grew from <strong>0.6% to 8%</strong>. That was the result of a business and its team working over time. It isn't a forecast for this pilot.</p>
      <p class="small">I've also worked through commercial challenges in fields as different as air testing, car parts, house moving and dentistry. I don't need to be the technical expert in your product. I do need enough access to understand how a customer buys it, and a person inside your business who can make a change.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section offer" aria-labelledby="pilot">
      <h2 id="pilot">The paid pilot</h2>
      <p class="price">NZ$1,500 <span>+ GST</span></p>
      <p>Two places. One commercial move per business. Paid upfront.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Focused pre-work review and one 90-minute working session</li>
        <li>A one-page brief with the decision, first action, owner and measure</li>
        <li>Five weekly 30-minute working calls and an end-of-pilot decision</li>
        <li>Up to eight hours of my time in total, within an agreed scope</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small">The aim is a useful decision and a real test early, followed by evidence about what happened. I won't promise a specific sales increase in six weeks.</p>
      <a class="action" href="#enquire">Enquire about the pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="enquire" aria-labelledby="enquire-title">
      <h2 id="enquire-title">Tell me what's happening</h2>
      <p>Give me enough context to see whether a conversation would be useful. I read every enquiry myself. Sending one doesn't commit you to the pilot.</p>
      <form id="next-move-enquiry">
        <div class="field"><label for="name">Your name</label><input id="name" name="name" autocomplete="name" required /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="email">Your email</label><input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="business">Business and your role</label><input id="business" name="business" required /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="success">If we were sitting here in 12 months, what would success look like?</label><textarea id="success" name="success" rows="3" required></textarea></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="stuck">Where do you think sales or customer follow-through is getting stuck?</label><textarea id="stuck" name="stuck" rows="3" required></textarea></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="tried">What have you tried so far?</label><textarea id="tried" name="tried" rows="2"></textarea></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="capacity">Can you or someone on your team act on one agreed move?</label><select id="capacity" name="capacity" required><option value="">Choose one</option><option>Yes</option><option>Possibly</option><option>No</option></select></div>
        <button class="action" type="submit">Prepare my email to Glenn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
        <p class="small">This opens your email app with your answers filled in. Review the message and press Send. If your email app doesn't open, <a href="mailto:glenn@spike.co.nz?subject=The%20Next%20Move%20enquiry">email me directly</a>.</p>
      </form>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#next-move-enquiry');
    form?.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      if (!form.reportValidity()) return;
      const data = new FormData(form);
      const get = (name: string) => String(data.get(name) ?? '').trim();
      const body = [
        `Name: ${get('name')}`,
        `Email: ${get('email')}`,
        `Business and role: ${get('business')}`,
        '',
        `Success in 12 months:\n${get('success')}`,
        '',
        `Where sales are getting stuck:\n${get('stuck')}`,
        '',
        `What I've tried:\n${get('tried') || 'Nothing yet'}`,
        '',
        `Capacity to act: ${get('capacity')}`,
      ].join('\n');
      window.location.href = `mailto:glenn@spike.co.nz?subject=${encodeURIComponent('The Next Move enquiry — ' + get('business'))}&body=${encodeURIComponent(body)}`;
    });
  </script>

  <style>
    .next-move { overflow-wrap: break-word; }
    .intro .eyebrow { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500; font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
    .intro h1 { margin-bottom: 1.35rem; }
    .lead { font-size: 1.12rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--text); }
    .next-move h2 { margin-top: 2.6rem; }
    .next-move .section { padding-top: .1rem; }
    .next-move .section h2 { margin-top: 1.7rem; }
    .action { display: inline-block; appearance: none; border: 1px solid var(--text); border-radius: 2px; background: var(--text); color: #fff; padding: .68rem 1rem; margin: 1rem 0 .45rem; font: 500 .9rem 'DM Sans', sans-serif; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; }
    .action:hover, .action:focus-visible { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; }
    .action span { margin-left: .65rem; }
    .small { font-size: .84rem; color: var(--mid); }
    .pull { font: 600 clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.8rem)/1.35 'Lora', Georgia, serif; color: var(--text); margin: 1.7rem 0; }
    .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; counter-reset: steps; }
    .steps li { counter-increment: steps; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1rem 0 1rem 2.35rem; position: relative; }
    .steps li::before { content: counter(steps, decimal-leading-zero); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent); font: 500 .75rem 'DM Sans', sans-serif; }
    .steps strong, .steps span { display: block; }
    .steps strong { color: var(--text); margin-bottom: .25rem; }
    .offer { border-top-color: var(--text); }
    .price { color: var(--text); font: 600 2.15rem 'Lora', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: .2rem 0 .45rem; }
    .price span { font: 400 .95rem 'DM Sans', sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0; }
    .field { margin: 1.1rem 0; }
    .field label { display: block; color: var(--text); font: 500 .9rem 'DM Sans', sans-serif; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
    .field input, .field textarea, .field select { display: block; width: 100%; border: 1px solid #b9b9b9; border-radius: 2px; padding: .62rem .7rem; background: #fff; color: var(--text); font: 400 1rem/1.5 'DM Sans', sans-serif; }
    .field textarea { resize: vertical; }
    .field input:focus, .field textarea:focus, .field select:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--link); outline-offset: 2px; }
    @media (max-width: 520px) { .action { width: 100%; } .steps li { padding-left: 2rem; } }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
